e  also won two consecutive golden globe  awards in 1967 and 1968 for co-starring  in the sand pebbles and dr doolittle  needless to say attenborough's career  contains no shortage of highlights and  his work will no doubt be familiar to  classic film fans younger film-goers  however have their own attenborough  memories thanks to his appearance as  john hammond whose ambitions led to the  creation of jurassic park that  blockbuster made him famous to a whole  new generation but it's just one short  chapter in a life of many great  cinematic achievements that ended on  august 24th 2014 at the age of 90.  would you talk about willis  kids of the 70s and 80s and honestly  anyone who enjoys the classic sitcoms of  the era will immediately recognize the  immortal catchphrase gary coleman coined  as an adorable kid on the long-running  hit sitcom different strokes coleman's  diminutive stature helped him continue  to play younger characters throughout  much of his career and at the peak of  his fame he landed a series of film and  television roles unfortunately his  youthful looks and peak height of 4 feet  8 inches were side effects of an  autoimmune kidney disease combined with  the medications he took throughout his  life to fight the condition  work in hollywood became harder to come  by after strokes left the airwaves and  behind the scenes he underwent frequent  dialysis treatments and was forced to  undergo two kidney transplants  after a fall at his home coleman died on  may 28 2010 of an epidural hematoma at  the age of 42.  exactly where you remember esteemed  actor edward herrmann from depends on  whether you favor musicals vampire  movies medical tv shows or fast-talking  mother-daughter family dramas  hermann is probably best recognized  today for his role as pompous but  warm-hearted patriarch richard gilmore  in the series gilmore girls richard's  dry sense of humor and quiet authority  contrasted with the quick wit and  constant banter that flew between his  daughter lorelei and his granddaughter  rory and his wife emily who was played  by kelly bishop off-screen hermann and  bishop both classically trained and  meticulous about their craft were  especially close herman's wife star whom  he married in 1994 would joke that  bishop was his other wife  in hermann's final moments his family  invited bishop to say goodbye with them  before his longest running role in  gilmore girls hermann worked regularly  on tv and in movies he was nominated for  an emmy for playing a priest in the  medical drama saint elsewhere and won  one for the legal series the practice  he played franklin d roosevelt in the  1982 adaptation of annie having  previously played the president for a  mini-series and tv movie in the late 70s  and in 1987 he played a stepfather from  literal hell in the vampire movie the  lost boys  hermann died of brain cancer at age 71  on december 31 2014  in the netflix revival of gilmore girls  it was revealed that richard had also  died sparking big changes for emily in  particular  deezer dee was one of the foundational  actors on hit medical trauma er  born darren thompson he played nurse  malik mcgrath on the show's entire  15-year run appearing in 188 episodes as  often happens in real hospitals as well  as fictional ones er typically focused  on its physicians and surgeons not the  nurses but thompson was one of just a  handful of actors who appeared in every  season and his episode count makes him  the fifth most prolific member of the  large cast  outside of er thompson had a few small  parts in movies including the cult  classic comedy romy and michelle's high  school reunion and appeared in vanilla  ice's video for cool as ice  he played one of the members of a  fictional rap group in the mockumentary  movie cb4 in 1993 and also rapped for  real he released multiple records  including the full-length album delayed  but not denied in 2008 and continued  making songs until his death his final  track history